    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Black Friday is the day after "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Thanksgiving",
            "zh": "感恩节"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in America. It is on the last Friday of November. The name was first used in the 1960s to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mark",
            "ref": "v-mark"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the beginning of the Christmas "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "holiday season",
            "zh": "假日季"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As the story goes, after "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "experiencing",
            "zh": "经历"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "losses",
            "ref": "v-loss"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " over the whole year, the stores would finally begin to make a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "profit",
            "ref": "v-profit"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on the day after Thanksgiving. Their "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "takings",
            "zh": "营收"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " went from being in the “red” to being in the “black”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "On Black Friday, many stores have big "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sales",
            "ref": "v-sale"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". You can see long "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "lines",
            "zh": "排队"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of people outside stores. They go shopping for the gifts they will give their family and friends on Christmas Day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Because of this, stores usually open around 6 a.m. in the morning. Some stores even open at "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "midnight",
            "ref": "v-midnight"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This makes Black Friday the busiest shopping day of the year."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "在过去，商家会用不同颜色的墨水来记账，账本上的红色表示亏损，黑色表示盈利。许多全年账面布满“赤字”的商家在感恩节(11月的第4个星期四)后的那一天终于扭亏为盈，账目从赤字转变为(黑色的)盈余，“黑色星期五”由此得名。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
